// @test: .to_string() in operand position is a canonical String (#216)
// @description: `x.to_string() == "22"` previously lowered the scalar to_string
//   result as a raw char* operand against a {ptr,i64} String literal and aborted
//   LLVM module verification ("Both operands to ICmp ... not of the same type").
//   A `.to_string()` expression must now always yield a full Vyb String struct
//   {ptr,i64}, so == / != in operand position typecheck and run.
// @category: ownership, codegen, string
// @expect: pass
// @expect-return: 0
main()<Int> -> {
    x<Int> = 22
    if (x.to_string() != "22") { return 1 }
    b<Bool> = true
    if (b.to_string() != "true") { return 2 }
    f<Float> = 2.5
    if (f.to_string() != "2.5") { return 3 }
    if (!(x.to_string() == "22")) { return 4 }
    return 0
}
